<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span><h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1><p>Answers to common questions about installation, accounts, AI, limits, security and the public website.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="section-inner">
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">01</span><h2>Does setup appear every time?</h2><p>No. The installer is intended for first-run setup. After the database, administrator and service configuration are completed, PocketCat writes an installation lock.</p><p>If the lock exists, the installer does not expose the setup form again. Administration is handled from the authenticated dashboard.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">02</span><h2>Can I use my own AWS credentials?</h2><p>Yes. The Bedrock settings page supports an API key as well as an AWS access key, secret access key and optional temporary session token.</p><p>When API-key authentication is not being used, the application can sign Bedrock requests with AWS Signature Version 4.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><h2>Can I choose a Bedrock model?</h2><p>Yes. The administrator can enter the Bedrock model ID and region. The application uses the Bedrock Converse API for compatible models and provides a compatible custom endpoint field.</p><p>Not every Bedrock model supports the same API contract. Models that do not support Converse may require a model-specific adapter or InvokeModel payload; the UI should therefore be treated as generic rather than a claim of identical behavior for every foundation model.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">04</span><h2>What is the free AI allowance?</h2><p>The current implementation uses an approximate 2 hours of active AI usage per day. The application estimates usage from text length instead of pretending to have exact provider tokenizer counts.</p><p>Once the daily active-time balance is exhausted, further AI requests are blocked until the daily reset or a higher plan is applied.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">05</span><h2>Can logged-in users view the public site?</h2><p>Yes. View Site opens the public landing page and other public pages normally. The homepage does not redirect an authenticated user back to the dashboard.</p><p>The public navigation also changes its authentication action to Dashboard when a user is already signed in.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">06</span><h2>Are the public counters live?</h2><p>Registered and active user counts come from the database. Task, note and project activity counters use stored application metrics and are incremented when new records are created.</p><p>The browser refreshes the public statistics endpoint periodically so the visible numbers can change without a full page reload.</p></article>
</div></section><section class="cta"><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#9db8ff">POCKETCAT</span><h2>Explore the workspace.</h2><p>See the product, create an account or contact the team when you are ready.</p><a class="btn" href="/signup/">Get Started</a></section><?php public_footer(); ?>